+Show the Configuration
+----------------------
+
+The :func:`config <cli.config_command>` command prints the loaded application's
+configuration as JSON. This is useful to check which values were actually
+loaded, for example when configuration comes from several sources such as
+``config.py``, environment variables, or instance folders. ::
+
+    $ flask --app hello config
+    {
+      "APPLICATION_ROOT": "/",
+      "DEBUG": false,
+      "SECRET_KEY": "***",
+      "TESTING": false
+    }
+
+Keys are sorted alphabetically and the output is indented so it is easy to
+read and diff.
+
+Values of keys that may contain sensitive information are masked with ``***``.
+A key is masked if its name contains ``SECRET``, ``PASSWORD``, ``TOKEN``, or
+``KEY``, ignoring case. For example ``SECRET_KEY``, ``MAIL_PASSWORD``, and
+``API_TOKEN`` are all masked. This makes it safer to paste the output into an
+issue report or share it with a colleague. Nested dictionaries are checked the
+same way.
+
+.. note::
+
+    Masking is based on key names only, so a custom key that holds a secret
+    but does not contain one of those words is still printed. Review the
+    output before sharing it.
+
+
